    "intro_html":  "Breakfast for dinner is not a compromise, it is a strategy. Eggs are the cheapest complete protein in the store, hash browns are the cheapest potato you can buy already shredded, and smoked turkey sausage brings the flavor without the price of bacon. This bakes into one pan and reheats beautifully, which most egg dishes cannot claim. Each serving runs 566 calories with \u003cstrong\u003e28 grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e$3.27\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost).",
